# Draft/publish gate (see docs/TESTING.md): `council draft` writes candidate
# snapshots here for investigator + defamation-auditor review — never
# committed, never served. `council publish` writes full-tier (private,
# paywall-pending) snapshots here — also never committed; only the
# public-tier subset it copies into frontend/public/data/ is meant to be
# public.
data/draft/
data/published_full/
data/reply_packets/

# council meeting-digest review artifact (docs/frontend/PRODUCT_ROADMAP.md
# F2) — deliberately separate from data/draft/ so it can never be mistaken
# for, or picked up by, the publish pipeline.
data/meeting_digest_preview/

.cache/

# Generated outputs
cost_report.txt
council.log

data/council.db-wal
data/council.db-shm

data/council.db.bak*

# Private strategy notes (track: strategy)
docs/strategy/

# private prompts
prompt_notes.txt

# Investigator-track OUTPUT docs (investigation findings, retroactive audits,
# session synthesis) are gitignored by default — these are the artefacts that
# name real individuals with risk-adjacent framing (recusal drivers, etc.),
# matching the risk PRIVATE_ASSESSMENT.md documents. This is an allow-list,
# not a per-filename deny-list, deliberately: a new investigation-output doc
# type (e.g. a future AUDIT_<date>.md from a Refiner sweep, or any other new
# session-output naming convention) is protected automatically, without
# needing this file updated every time one is invented. Only the governing
# prompt/protocol docs — methodology, not findings — are explicitly
# un-ignored below. `INVESTIGATIONS.md` specifically: kept locally, not
# removed from git history — see the commit that untracked it for what that
# means.
docs/investigator/*.md
!docs/investigator/EXPLORATION_PROTOCOL.md
!docs/investigator/REFINEMENT_PROTOCOL.md
# design artefact, names no individuals — safe to track, unlike the output docs above
!docs/investigator/COVERAGE_AUDIT_2026-08-23.md
